WEBVTT

00:00:11.159 --> 00:00:14.226
Build an equipment quantity form that explains

00:00:14.226 --> 00:00:17.692
rejected input while preserving the last valid saved

00:00:17.692 --> 00:00:18.092
value.

00:00:18.092 --> 00:00:21.359
We will test the actual controls in the Workspace

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:24.159
Desktop with both the button and keyboard.

00:02:11.201 --> 00:02:13.591
QuantityModel holds the saved state.

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:17.111
The candidate is a proposed value, separate from that

00:02:17.111 --> 00:02:17.509
state.

00:02:17.509 --> 00:02:21.095
Trim removes surrounding spaces, and parseInt attempts

00:02:21.095 --> 00:02:22.091
a whole number.

00:02:22.091 --> 00:02:25.145
A parse failure produces a correction message.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:28.598
A parsed number outside one through five returns the

00:02:28.598 --> 00:02:30.988
range message before the assignment.

00:02:30.988 --> 00:02:33.976
Only an accepted candidate replaces quantity.

00:02:34.397 --> 00:02:36.524
A TextField holds editable text.

00:02:36.524 --> 00:02:39.581
Its associated Label states the allowed range;

00:02:39.581 --> 00:02:42.572
setLabelFor connects that label to its input.

00:02:42.572 --> 00:02:45.895
Submission is the deliberate action that reads the

00:02:45.895 --> 00:02:48.752
current text and asks the model to save it.

00:02:48.752 --> 00:02:52.142
One EventHandler is registered with both the button

00:02:52.142 --> 00:02:53.072
and the field.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.395
Button activation and Enter therefore use the same

00:02:56.395 --> 00:02:58.522
validation and visible feedback.

00:02:58.662 --> 00:03:01.912
The field starts with two, but no submission has

00:03:01.912 --> 00:03:02.522
happened.

00:03:02.522 --> 00:03:04.756
Predict the initial console line.

00:03:04.756 --> 00:03:08.277
After saving two, should a word, zero or six replace

00:03:08.277 --> 00:03:09.361
the saved value?

00:03:09.361 --> 00:03:12.611
Trace the returns and assignment before running.

00:03:12.611 --> 00:03:13.762
Pause and decide.

00:03:28.432 --> 00:03:31.795
The initial console reports saved quantity zero.

00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:35.298
The field contains two and the status says nothing

00:03:35.298 --> 00:03:35.719
saved.

00:03:35.719 --> 00:03:39.432
Text waiting in a field is not yet saved model state.

00:03:43.977 --> 00:03:46.954
The button submission now displays Saved two.

00:03:46.954 --> 00:03:50.130
We will replace the input with a word and submit

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:50.527
again.

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:05.713
The form asks for a whole number from one to five.

00:04:05.713 --> 00:04:09.085
Parsing failed before the assignment, so the saved

00:04:09.085 --> 00:04:10.299
value remains two.

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:13.536
Now test the two values just outside the allowed

00:04:13.536 --> 00:04:13.941
range.

00:04:24.237 --> 00:04:26.737
Zero receives the range message.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.536
Six receives the same range message.

00:04:39.536 --> 00:04:42.897
Both inputs were numbers, but neither reached the

00:04:42.897 --> 00:04:43.652
assignment.

00:04:43.652 --> 00:04:47.287
The feedback changes while the saved value stays two.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:50.443
Shift Tab returns keyboard focus to the field.

00:04:50.443 --> 00:04:53.392
Replace its text with five and press Enter.

00:05:01.044 --> 00:05:04.729
Enter displays Saved five through the shared handler.

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:08.067
A valid submission still works after the errors.

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:11.544
The console remains the initial report; the status

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.769
label shows these later results.

00:05:15.911 --> 00:05:19.424
If you moved the quantity assignment before the range

00:05:19.424 --> 00:05:22.607
check, what saved value would survive an invalid

00:05:22.607 --> 00:05:23.137
attempt?

00:05:23.137 --> 00:05:26.584
Choose a valid, invalid, then valid sequence to test

00:05:26.584 --> 00:05:27.711
your explanation.
